    "title": "Severe storms lead to fireworks show cancellation in Watertown - NewsBreak",
    "text": "By Dan Mount ,\n2 hours ago\nWATERTOWN, N.Y. (WWTI) – Mother Nature decided to put on her own fireworks display in Jefferson County.\nAround 7:30 p.m. the City of Watertown, Jefferson County Emergency Management, and Watertown Noon Rotary made the choice to cancel the fireworks and concert at Thompson Park as part of the city’s Fourth of July celebration.\n“This difficult decision was made after consultations with the National Weather Service Office in Buffalo and local weather forecasters,” said an announcement from the city regarding the cancelation.\nA Severe Thunderstorm Warning was issued for the county around 8 p.m. and storms did pass through the area.\nThe announcement didn’t say if the fireworks would take place at a later date.\nLatest Stories\nCopyright 2026 Nexstar Media, Inc. All rights reserved. This material may not be published, broadcast, rewritten, or redistributed. For the latest news, weather, sports, and streaming video, head to WWTI - InformNNY.com.",
    "summary": "WATERTOWN, N.Y. (WWTI) – Mother Nature decided to put on her own fireworks display in Jefferson County. Around 7:30 p.m. the City of Watertown, Jefferson County Emergency Management, and Watertown Noon Rotary made the choice to cancel the fireworks and concert at Thompson Park as part of the city’s Fourth of July celebration. “This difficult decision was made after consultations with the National Weather Service Office in Buffalo and local weather forecasters,” said an announcement from the city regarding the cancelation. A Severe Thunderstorm Warning was issued for the county around 8 p.m. and storms did pass through the area.",
